BWIGLEY wrote:
> Identifying in nethack can already take quite a while.  If it was made
> any harder it could put people off nethack.  I know on RGRD one of the
> reasons some people don't like nethack is the time spent IDing.
> Although I don't mind doing it IMHO if the process took any longer it
> would start being the center of the game.

Some, including myself, would argue that it SHOULD be the center of the
game.  It was the center of Rogue and the thing that added the most
interest to that game.

Once a player knows what all the important items in the game are, he's
most of the way towards winning.  I would put that moment off for as
long as possible.

Anyway, Nethack's design should not be, and isn't, steered by what
would put people off the game.  Here's a koan for you: if it were, it'd
be a lot less interesting.

